World model: Clicking a pink tile (the last attempted action) did not change orange or pink counts; the board state remained the same (no new orange nodes, no removal). Goal model: Still unclear – orange tiles persist despite clicks on orange, white, or pink. Perhaps the goal is to create a specific pattern or clear all non‑background colors. Open questions: What action causes any reduction in colored objects? Does clicking a magenta (M) tile have effect? Plan: Test clicking a magenta tile (there are 2 M nodes).
